tortoise-wow: VMaNGOS Eluna methods that write server-wide state are world-only.

A map's Lua state runs on that map's update thread, next to the other maps'
updates (one world state + one state per map/instance; World::GetEluna already
refuses the world state off the world thread). Some methods in the VMaNGOS
global method table write data outside their map: PerformIngameSpawn (FindMap of
any map, map->Add, ObjectMgr::AddCreatureToGrid), SendMail (an online receiver
on any map), SaveAllPlayers, StartGameEvent/StopGameEvent (spawn and despawn on
all maps), AddVendorItem/VendorRemoveItem/VendorRemoveAllItems, AddTaxiPath,
Kick and Ban (session and account layer), Player:KickPlayer (the same
WorldSession::KickPlayer call as the global Kick: it closes the socket of a
session, which the network threads own, from a map thread), and
Player:LogoutPlayer (WorldSession::LogoutPlayer deletes the player
synchronously while the calling hook's C++ frames may still hold it). Called
from a map state they run on that map's thread next to other maps and their
sessions.

They are now flagged METHOD_REG_WORLD, the mechanism Eluna's multistate mode
already uses for the Group and Guild methods (methods/VMangos/GroupMethods.h
"GetMembers", "SetLeader", "Disband", ...; GuildMethods.h likewise): the state
registers ElunaTemplate<T>::MethodWrongState instead of the method, and a call
raises "attempt to call method '...' that does not exist for state: N". The
world state, which runs on the world thread while no map updates, keeps them.

Upstreamable: the CMangos backend already flags several of its global functions
world-only and VMaNGOS' table flagged none.

Base: ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna 1b06f28ff3a00054d915d824c725fb4283fee74d (branch
cmangos-spell-update), the dep/Eluna pin, with patches 0001-0008 applied. Eluna is
GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna, LICENSE); this change is under
the same licence. Applied by cmake/ElunaSources.cmake to a copy in the build tree.
